# Virtual-machine guest integration.
#
# Three of the four public reviewers of Shadowfetch ran it in a VM, and one had
# to open System Settings and set 1280x800 by hand because the guest had no way
# to negotiate a resolution with the host. The 2.0.0 manifest listed 3332
# packages and not one matched spice, qemu, virtualbox or open-vm, so there was
# no dynamic resolution, no clipboard sharing and no guest-agent shutdown.
#
# EVERY package here was verified present in Debian testing by grepping the
# chroot apt lists, not the build host. An earlier revision of this file listed
# virtualbox-guest-x11, xserver-xorg-video-qxl and xserver-xorg-video-vmware,
# which were checked against the build box (Ubuntu) instead of the target
# (Debian testing) and do not exist there. That broke the 2.0.1 build at
# chroot_package-lists.install with "Unable to locate package".
#
# NOT included, and why:
#   virtualbox-guest-x11 / virtualbox-guest-utils - not packaged in Debian
#     testing. VirtualBox users still need the Oracle Guest Additions ISO, so
#     VirtualBox auto-resize is a documented limitation rather than something
#     this list can fix. /linux/hardware should say so plainly.
#   xserver-xorg-video-qxl / xserver-xorg-video-vmware - removed from Debian;
#     the kernel modesetting driver covers both.
#
# All of these are inert on bare metal: their services do not start without the
# matching hypervisor present.
spice-vdagent
qemu-guest-agent
open-vm-tools
